# feat(logging): add file logging via LogFolderPath

## Summary

Adds an opt-in way to capture IRT's diagnostic logging to disk. Set a new
`LogFolderPath` config value to a folder and every `Write-PSFMessage` call (all
levels) is written to `<LogFolderPath>\IRT-<date>.log` — a new file per day, with
files older than 30 days pruned automatically. Leave it blank and nothing
changes; file logging stays off. There's no size limit and no compression by
design — just a clean, dated text log you can hand off with an investigation or
tail while troubleshooting a failed connection.

This is built entirely on PSFramework's native `logfile` logging provider, so
none of the ~500 existing `Write-PSFMessage` call sites had to change — enabling
the provider once routes them all to the file.

## What changed

- **New `LogFolderPath` config setting** (`ConfigTemplate.json`). `null`/blank =
  off; a folder path = on. Backfills automatically into existing user configs.
- **`Initialize-IRTFileLogging`** (new private helper) enables or disables the
  `logfile` provider to match `LogFolderPath`. Output is TXT, one file per day
  (`IRT-%Date%.log`), with `LogRetentionTime` set to 30 days. A mutex lets
  multiple IRT windows share a folder safely.
- **Applied in two places** so it always reflects the current setting: at module
  load (`Suffix.ps1`) and from `Set-IRTConfig`. Changing the folder in the config
  menu now takes effect immediately — no module reimport required.
- **`Set-IRTConfig` menu entry** ("Debug log folder") with guidance that it wants
  a folder, shows the resulting `IRT-<date>.log` name, and notes the change
  applies right away.
- **Runspace workers are intentionally skipped** when enabling the provider. The
  playbook's workers are in-process runspaces that share PSFramework's
  process-wide logging queue, so the main session's provider already captures
  their messages; enabling 15+ duplicate providers would only race on the file
  and log rotation.
- Rebuilt root artifacts (`M365IncidentResponseTools.psm1`,
  `Data/ConfigTemplate.json`) are included.

## Also in this PR (separate commit)

`fix(debug): make debug harness worktree-aware` — `Find-ModuleRoot` previously
located the module root by matching a folder to a same-named `.psd1`, which fails
inside a git worktree (the folder is named for the branch). It now resolves the
expected manifest name from the main working tree. The `_DEBUG` scripts were
updated to a `$RepoRoot` variable name and a `Connect-IRTT` typo was corrected to
`Connect-IRT` so the harness imports and connects correctly from a worktree.

## Testing

- **Offline Pester**: 417 passed, 2 skipped, 1 failure. The lone failure is
  `Get-IRTClipboardSearch` ("Expected 'OnlyOne', but got 'O'"), which is unrelated
  to this change and pre-existing on the branch — no logging code touches it.
- **Online Pester**: not run here (requires interactive Graph/Exchange auth).
- **Formatting**: all checks (`Formatting` category) pass on every changed source
  file — 0 findings.
- **Manual verification**: confirmed the provider enables on set and writes
  `IRT-<date>.log` inside the folder; that clearing the folder stops logging live;
  that message levels 1–9 are all captured; and that a worker running in a
  playbook-style in-process runspace lands its messages in the same file.

